  "id": "COMPOUND:31782 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Beta-Himachalene is implicated in the biological activity of HL-60 cells, which are a type of leukemia cell line. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which lead to the target Neuropilin-2. The evidence suggests that beta-Himachalene acts as a target for HL-60 cells, which in turn are targeted by various compounds, including (10S)-10-methylheptadecanoic acid and (2R)-2-[4-(7-Chloroquinoxalin-2-Yl)Oxyphenoxy]Propanoic Acid. These compounds are all linked to Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which beta-Himachalene may influence Neuropilin-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The shared target of HL-60 cells across these different compounds suggests a broader role for these molecules in cellular signaling pathways, potentially linking beta-Himachalene to Neuropilin-2 through a common cellular mechanism.",
